# Test-target overrides. SwiftFormat uses the closest config file to each input,
# so this applies to financeplanTests/ only and leaves app code on the root rules.

# Do NOT strip `async` / `throws` from test methods that contain no await or try.
#
# XCTest invokes a synchronous test method off the main thread. In a @MainActor
# test class that trips Swift 6's actor-isolation check, and the process aborts
# with SIGABRT *after* the test body has already run — xcodebuild reports it with
# no failure message at all, so it reads as an unexplained crash.
#
# Marking such tests `async` is the fix, but redundantAsync removes the keyword
# again the moment nobody awaits anything, silently reintroducing the abort. That
# is how 64 tests across 11 suites ended up failing at once.
#
# Tests here also carry an explicit `await Task.yield()` so they survive a
# formatter run that predates this file.
--disable redundantAsync
--disable redundantThrows
--disable redundantTypedThrows
